            <ArticleTitle>Rib xanthoma resected by video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery using a bone punch.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e15-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/SLE.0b013e318188c2f3</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Xanthomas of the rib are extremely rare benign neoplasms, most commonly reported in soft tissue, but rarely in bone. We report a case of a 4-cm xanthoma of the rib resected by video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery and pulled through a 2-cm port incision around the patient's areola. To the best of our knowledge, there are only 8 other such cases, and none of which were removed by thoracoscopic surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
